on (b). Dilute 1.0 ml of reference solution (a) \nto 10.0 ml with solution A.\nInject reference solution (a) and the test solution. In the \nchromatogram obtained with the test solution the area of any \nsecondary peak is not more than the area of the principal peak \nin the chromatogram obtained with reference solution (a) \n(1.0 per cent), the sum of areas of all the secondary peaks is \nnot more than 3.5 times the area of the principal peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (a) (3.5 per \ncent). Ignore any peak with an area less than 0.05 times the \narea of the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained with\nReference solution (c). A0.15 per cent w/v solution of cefdinir \nRS and 0.01 per cent solution of cefdinir impurity A RS initially\nCefdinir\nin diluent and then with solution A.\nChromatographic system\nO\nOH\n-\na stainless steel column 15 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with \noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 gm), \n-\ncolumn temperature: 40° \n-\nmobile phase: A. a mixture of 1000 ml of solution A and \nadd 0.4 ml of solution B.\nN \tCH2\nreference solution (a) (0.05 per cent).\n•\nBacterial endotoxins (2.2.3). Not more than 0.15 Endotoxin \nUnit per mg of cefazolin.\nH2N\nH\nB. a mixture of 300 volumes of acetonitrile, \n200 volumes of methanol, 500 volumes of a solution A \nand 0.4 volumes of solution B. \n-\nflow rate: 1 ml per minute,\nWater (2.3.43). Not more than 6.0 per cent, determined on 0.15\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\ni3N505S2\nSolution A._ Prepare by dissolving 0.75 g of salicylic \n(internal standard) in 5 ml ofmethanol and diluting to 1\n• 't, 3-95 -4 \t\n-a gradient programme using the conditions given below,\n r is 5-thia 1-azabicyclo[4.2.0]oct-2- \nacid.\nrbOtylic_ \t\n-§pectrophotometer set at 254 nm, \n-.\n.-- injection volume: 10\nwith mixed phosphate buffer pH 7.0.\n•_\nCEFDINIR\nMobile phase A\nTime \n(in min.)\n(per cent v/v)\n0 \n95 \n5\n2 \n95 \n5\n22 \n75 \n25\n32 \n50 \n50\n37 \n5