d with \noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (3 pm) (Such \nas Kingsorb C 18), \n-\ncolumn temperature: 40°, \n-\nmobile phase: A. a 0.476 per cent w/v solution of \npotassium dihydrogen orthophosphate, adjusted to\n' 56-0-methylerythromycin A (E)-9-(0-methyloxime),\n\"63\"-N-demethy1-3'-N-formy1-6-0-methylerythromycin A. \nInject reference solution (b) and the test solution. I n the \nchromatogram obtained with the test solution, the area of any \nsecondary peak is not more than the area of the peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (b) (1 .0 per \ncent) and the sum of areas of all the secondary peaks is not \nmore than 3.5 times the area of the peak in the chromat ogram \nobtained with reference solution (b) (3.5 per cent). Ignore any \npeak with an area less than 0.2 times of the principal peak \nobtained with reference solution (b) (0.2 per cent).\nClarithromycin Tablets\nClarithromycin Tablets contain not less than 90.0 per cent and \nnot more than 1110.0 per \nper cent of the stated amount of\npH 4.4 with orthophosphoric acid or potassium \nhydroxide solution,\ncla\nclarithromycin,C38\nUsual strengths. 250 mg; 500 mg.\nB. acetonitrile, \n-\na gradient programme using the conditions given below, \nflow rate: 1.1 ml per minute, \n-\nspectrophotometer set at 205 nm, \ninjection volume: 10 ttl."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/clarithromycin","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Clarithromycin"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Clarithromycin\nC38H69NO13 \nMol. Wt. 748.0\nClarithromycin is (3R,4S,5S,6R,1R,9R, nR,12R,13S,14Rf \n4-[(2,6-Dideoxy-3-C-methyl-3-O-methyl-a-L-ribo-hexo- \npyrano sy l)oxy] -14-ethy 1-1.2,13-dihy droxy-7-methoxy- 3,5, \n7,9,1 l,13-hexamethyl-6-[[3,4,6-trideoxy-3-(dimethyIamino)- \noc-D-xylo-hexopyranosyl]oxy]oxacyclotetradecane-2,10-dione (6- \nO-methylerythromycin A).\nClarithromycin contains not less than 96.0 per cent and not \nmore than 102.0 per cent of C3gH69NOi3, calculated on the \nanhydrous basis.\nCategory. Antibacterial.\nDescription. A white or almost white, crystalline powder."},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Clarithromycin\nC38H69NO13 \nMol. Wt. 748.0\nClarithromycin is (3R,4S,5S,6R,1R,9R, nR,12R,13S,14Rf \n4-[(2,6-Dideoxy-3-C-methyl-3-O-methyl-a-L-ribo-hexo- \npyrano sy l)oxy] -14-ethy 1-1.2,13-dihy droxy-7-methoxy- 3,5, \n7,9,1 l,13-hexamethyl-6-[[3,4,6-trideoxy-3-(dimethyIamino)- \noc-D-xylo-hexopyranosyl]oxy]oxacyclotetradecane-2,10-dione (6- \nO-methylerythromycin A).\nClarithromycin contains not less than 96.0 per cent and not \nmore than 102.0 per cent of C3gH69NOi3, calculated on the \nanhydrous basis.\nCategory. Antibacterial.\nDescription. A white or almost white, crystalline powder."},{"name":"Identification","text":"Determine by infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2.4.6). \nCompare the spectrum with that obtained with clarithromycin \nIPRS or with the reference spectrum of clarithromycin.\nIn the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained \nwith the test solution corresponds to the peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with the reference solution."},{"name":"Tests","text":"Specific optical rotation (2.4.22). -102° to - 94°, determined on a 1 \nper cent w/v solution in dichloromethane at 20°.\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography \n(2.4.14).\nTest solution. Dissolve 75 mg of the substance under \nexamination in 25 ml of acetonitrile and dilute to 50.0 ml with \nwater.\nReference solution (a). Dissolve 7.5 mg of clarithromycin \nIPRS in 2.5 ml of acetonitrile and dilute to 5.0 ml with water.\nReference solution (b). Dilute 1.0 ml of reference solution (a) to\n100.0 ml with equal volumes of acetonitrile and water.\nUse chromatographic system as, described under Assay. ,\nInject reference solution (b). the test is not valid unless the \ntailing factor is not more than 2.0. \n- - '\n2021\nName\nRelative \nretention time\nCorrection\"'\nfactor\nClarithromyc