taining immunoglobulins, mainly IgG. Other \nproteins may be present. Human normal immunoglobulin \ncontains the IgG antibodies of normal subjects. It is intended \nfor intramuscular or subcutaneous administration.\n[Pyrogens. Complies with the test for pyrogens. Inject per kg\n[ofthe rabbit’s mass"},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Complex\nmg of total protein, before the addition of any \namount Prote^n by multiplying the result\nstabilizer. \n.....\nCategory. Coagulation factor. \n\\\nThe factor IX fraction is dissolved in a suitable liquid, \nsome products, especially those without a protein\nanti-thrombin and other auxiliary substances svic^i^lfiepsuch as albumin, this method may not be applicable. \nstabilizer may be included. No anti-microbial pr&serva^^er validated method for protein determination must \nadded. The solution is passed through a bacteriax'Qt^Sfi¡grrfprf'be performed.\nfilter, distributed aseptically into the final contain»coagulation faetor(2.8.3),ifnecessary, dilute the \nimmediately frozen It is subsequently freeze-dried \nexamination t0 contain 20 IU of factor IX\ncontainers are closed under vaccum or under an inert \nofthe dilution the coagulation timéis not less\nIt is a sterile, freeze dried powder consisting of partially purified \nFactor IX fraction, as well as concentrated factors II, VII and \nX fractions, of venous plasma obtained from healthy human \ndonors. It contains no preservative.\nIt complies with the requirements of the test for potency in \nhaving not less than 80.0 per cent and not more than 120.0 per \ncent of the potency stated on the label in factor IX Units by \ncomparison with the factor IX standard or with a working \nreference that has been calibrated with it.\nConsistency ofthe method \n: .gthaiiiSO seconds.\njgeparin (2.8 9). If heparin has been added during preparation, \n^termine-.the. amount by the assay of heparin in coagulation \n^factot concentrates. The preparation under examination\nThe consistency 