es.\nWithdraw a suitable volume of the medium and filter.\nDetermine by liquid chromatography (2:4.14).\nTest solution. Use the filtrate and dilute further with dissolution \nmedium, if necessary.\nReference solution. A O.OOl.per cent w/y sqlutiqn of \nrepaglinide IPRSm. methanol. Dilute 5.0 ml of the solution to\n100.0 ml with the dissolution medium. ' ' ' '\nChromatographic system r...\n- a stainless steel column 12.5 cm x 4 mm, packed with\n: 1 octadccylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 pm), ‘ ;: \\:\n• column temperature: 40°,\n■ mobile phase: a mixture of 49 volumes of acetonitrile,\n40 Volumes of0.15per cent w/vof monobasicpotassium \nphosphate solution, adjusted to pH 2.3 with drtho- \nphosphoric acid and11 volumes of methanol,f ; i ' \n'' -' flow rate: 1 ml per minute, ■! ;:-1 ■ -; ;: '\n- fluorometric detector: excitation wavelength of244 nm\nand emission wavelength of348 nm, \n- injection volume: 20 pl.\nInject the reference solution. The test is riot valid unless the \nrelative standard deviation for replicate injections is; not more \nthan 2.0 per cent and the tailing factor is not; more than 2.0.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution. ; ..\nCalculate the content of ^HjeN^O^in the medium. \n'\nQ. Not less than 70 per cent of the stated amount of \nC27H36N?.O4. \n' \n\" 1 \n’\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid, chromatography \n(2.4.14) as described under Assay with the foiloWing \nmodifications. \n* b-Gvoo/q wed\n3472\n2022i|\nReference solution (d). Dilute 2.5 ml of reference solution (b) / \nto 1000 ml with the solvent mixture. .. . v; . \n, J\n- spectrophotometer set at 210 nm, ' m ; \n; \n)\nInject reference solution (c) and (d). The test is.not valid unless i \nthe resolution between the peaks, due to repaglinide and ' \nrepaglinide impurity A is not less than 7.0 and the tailing factor \nis not more than 2.0 in the chromatogram obtained with \nreference solution (c) and the relative standard deviation for \nreplicate injections is not more than 10.0 per cent in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (d).\nInject the test solution. The sum of areas of all the secondary \npeaks is not more than 0.5 per; cent,. ;calculated?by area \nnormalisation. \n... \nm\nOther tests. .Comply with the tests stated under Tablets.\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nSolvent mixture. 70 volumes of methanol and 30 volumes of \n0.2 per cent w/v of monobasic ammonium phosphate solution, \nadjusted to pH 4.0 with orthophosphoric acid.\nTest solution. Disperse 8 intact tablets in the solvent mixture \nand dilute to obtain a solution containing 0.008 per cent w/v \nof Repaglinide in the solvent mixture, stir for 20 minutes and \nfilter. \n; oy Colma-- yrerme wd\nReference solution (a): A 0.08 per cent w/v solution of \nrepaglinide IPRS in methanol. '\"ri'\nReference solution (b). Dilute 5.0 ml of reference solution (aj\nto 50.0 ml with the solvent mixture. ■ ' 1 y ; yv; ■;\nReference solution (c). A 0.008 per cent w/v solution of \nrepaglinide impurity A IPRS (4~(carbdxymethyl)-2-eih6ty- \nbenzoic acid IPRS) in methanol. To 1.0 nil of the solutibii, add \n5.0; ml of reference solution (a) and dilute to 50.0 ml with, the \nsolvent mixture. \n\\ ■ IJ-A\nChromatographic system . ■ - ;. \n, v \n/\n- a stainless steel column 6.0 cm x 4 mm, packed, with\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 gm), /. < /;.;i \n- column temperature: 40°, \nt.\n- mobile phase: a mixture of 70volumes of methanol and\n30 volumes of 0.2 per cent W/v solution of monobasic \nv ; >• ammonium:phosphate, adjusted to pH 2.5 with\northophosphoric acid, ■ ; ■ ■ ■. >.• :■ ; J iv: ”4*1 G\n- flow rate: 1 ml per minute, \n; ,.......\n- spectrophotometer set at 245 nm,\ninjection volume: 20 pl.\nInject reference solution (b) and (c). The test is not valid unless \nthe resolution between the peaks due-to. repaglinide and \nrepaglinide impurity A is not less than 7.0, the tailing factor is \nnot more than .2.0 m the chrom