ore; than 0.3 times the area of the principal peak in the \nchmrnatogram obtained with reference solution (a) (0.3 per \ncent). The area of any peak due to impurity A and impurity E, \neach of, is not more than 0.2 times the area of the principal \npeak iri the chromatogram obtained with reference solution \n(a)(0.2per cent), the area of any peak due to impurity B, \nmultiplied by correction factor 2.0 and impurity b,each of, is \nnot more than 0.4 times the area of the principal peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (a) (0.4 per \ncen0- The area of any other secondary peak is not morethan"}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/ritodrine-injection","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Ritodrine Injection"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Ritodrine Injection\nRitodrine Hydrochloride-Inj ection\nRitodrine Injection is a sterile solution of Ritodrine \nHydrochloride in Water for Injections.\nRitodrine Injection contains not less than 93.0 per cent and \nnot more than 105.0 per cent of the stated amount of ritodrine \nhydrochloride; C17H21NO3,HCI.\nUsual strength. 10 mg per ml.\nA. Dilute a suitable volume of the injection with methanol \n(30 per cent) to obtain a solution containing 0.01 per cent\nw/v of Ritodrine Hydrochloride. When examined in the range \n230 nm to 350 nm (2.4.7) exhibits a maximum at 275 nm and a \nshoulder at about280nm. \n?;\nB. In the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with the test solution corresponds to the principal\n3505\nwww.webofpharma.com\npeak in the chromatogram obtained with reference solution"},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Ritodrine Injection\nRitodrine Hydrochloride-Inj ection\nRitodrine Injection is a sterile solution of Ritodrine \nHydrochloride in Water for Injections.\nRitodrine Injection contains not less than 93.0 per cent and \nnot more than 105.0 per cent of the stated amount of ritodrine \nhydrochloride; C17H21NO3,