ss than 90.Ó per cent and not\npiore than 1Ì0 Ò Pcr cent of the stated amount of sildenafil,\nUsual strengths, 25 mg; 50 mg; 100 mg."},{"name":"Identification","text":"In the Assays the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained \nwith the test solution corresponds to the peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with the reference solution.\nTests' '.J.;,\nDissolution (2.5.2).\nApparatus No. 2 (Paddle),\nMedium. 900 ml of0;0 PM Hydrochloric acid,\nSpeed and time. 100 rpm and 30 minute s.\nWithdraw a suitablevolume of the medium and filter. Measure \nthe absorbance of the filtered solution, suitably diluted with \nthe medium if necessary, at the; maximum at about 294 nm \n(2.4.7),; Calculatethe content of C22H3oN604S in the medium \nfrom the absorbance obtained from a solution of known \nconcentration &f,sildenafil citrate IPRS in the same medium.\nQ, NÓti!Ìèisisithan\":70 per cent of the stated ainount'of\nC&HjoNgOiS.\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography \n(2.4.14)\nSolvent mixture. 50 volumes of mobile phase A and 50 volumes \nof methanol.\n■■ ■ \n< .'fir ,\nTestsolution.Weigh and powder 20 tablets. Disperse a quantity \nof powder containing about 50 mg of sildenafil with 35 ml of \nthe solvent mixture, sonicate for 20 minutes and dilute to 50 ml \nwith the solvent mixture, filter.\nReferèncésolution (a). A 0.028 per cent w/v solution of \nùktenqfU citrate IPRS in the solvent mixture.\nReference solution (b). Dilute 5.0 ml of reference solution (a) \n10100 ml with the solvent mixture.\nChromatographic system\n“ a stainless steel column 25 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\noctadecylsilane chemically bonded to porous silica \n(5 itm)(Such as Zorbax Eclipse XDB Cl 8), \n~ c°lumn temperature: 40°,\n’■ mobilephase: A. a solution containing 3.85 g of\n^’ dmmoniùm acetate, and 1.0 ml of triethylamine in 1000\nadjusted to pH 5.5 with acetic acid, \ns-.;; \n■ y methanol,\n- a gradient programme using the conditions given below,\n- flow rate: 1 ml per minute,\n- \nspectrophotometer set at 294 nm, o\n- injection volume:10 pl.\nTime\nMobile Phase A\nMobile Phase B\n(in min.)\n(per cent, /v/v)\n, . (per. cent./v/v)\n0\n47\n53\n20\n47\n53 .\n35\n10\n■ ■ . 90 : - .\n45\n10\n90\n50\n47\n53\n60\n, 47 .\n53 . \n;\nInject reference solution (b). The test is not valid unless the \nrelative standard deviation for replicate injections is not more\nthan 5.0 per cent.\nInject reference solution (b) and the test solution. In the \nchromatogram obtained with the test solution, the area of any \nsecondary peak is not more than 0.8 times the area of the \nprincipal peak in the chromatogram obtained with reference \nsolution (b) (0.8 per cent), the area of peak corresponding to \nN-oxide impurity at relative retention time 0.54 is not more \nthan the area of the principal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with reference solution (b) (1.0 per cent) and the sum \nof areas of all the secondary peaks is not more than 2.0 times \nthe area of the peak in the chromatogram obtained with \nreference solution (b) (2.0 per cent). Ignore the peak due to \ncitric acid at retention time about 2.4 minutes: v v. ..\nOther tests. Comply with the tests stated under Tablets.\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nSolvent mixture. 50 volumes of mobile phase and 50 volumes \nof methanol.\nTest solution. Weigh and powder 20 tablets. Disperse a quantity \nof powder containing about 50 mg of sildenafil with 35 ml of \nthe solvent mixture, sonicate for 20 minutes and dilute to \n50.0 ml with the solvent mixture, filter.\nReference solution. A 0.14 per cent w/v solution of sildenafil \ncitrate IPRS in the solvent mixture.\nChromatographic system\n- a stainless steel column 25 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\nsilica (5 pm) (Such as Zorbax Eclipse XDB C 1.8), ?\n- mobile phase: a mixture of 30 volumes of solution\ncontaining 3.85 g of ammonium acetate and 1.0 ml of \ntriethylamine in 1000 ml of -water,, adjusted to pH 5.5 \nwith acetic acid and 70 volumes of methanol, ■\n- flow rate: 1 ml per minute, ..\n- spectrophotometer set at 294 nm,\ninjection volume: 20 pl.\n3579\nwww.webofpharma.com\nCOLLOIDAL SILICON DIOXIDE\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the \ntheoretical plates is not less than 2000, the tailing factor is not \nmore than 2.0 and the relative standard deviation for replicate\ninjections is not more than 2.0 per cent. -\nInject the deference solution thé'test solution.\nCalcúlate the content of C22I l30N6O4S in the tablet?\nStorage. Store protected from moisture.\nLabelling. The label states the strength in terms of the \nequivalent amount of sildenafil."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/silver-nitrate","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Silver Nitrate"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Silver Nitrate\nAgNO: \nMol. Wt. 169.9 |\nLoss on ignition represents the amount of S iO2 iri the amount | \nof the substance taken for the test for Loss on ignition, / \n|\nStorage. Store protected from light. \n■■ - ■ g\nSilver Nitrate contains not less than 99.0 per cent and not \nmore than 100.5 per cent of AgNO3. 1 \n; \n?|\nCategory. Local anti-infective. , \n. ;,7... '■ '/i\nDescription. Cplourless.cjystals or a white, crystalline powder, ¿g"},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Silver Nitrate\nAgNO: \nMol. Wt. 169.9 |\nLoss on ignition represents the amount of S iO2 iri the amount | \nof the substance taken for the test for Loss on ignition, / \n|\nStorage. Store protected from light. \n■■ - ■ g\nSilver Nitrate contains not less than 99.0 per cent and not \nmore than 100.5 per cent of AgNO3. 1 \n; \n?|\nCategory. Local anti-infective. , \n. ;,7... '■ '/i\nDescription. Cplourless.cjystals or a white, crystalline powder, ¿g"},{"name":"Identification","text":"4\nA. It gives the reactions of silver salts (2.3.1). \n.¡w\nB. 10 mg gives reaction (A) of nitrates (2.3.1). \n.\nTests ' \n:'-g\nAppearance of solution. A 4.0 per cent w/v solu