ure of 70 volumes of chloroform, \n40 volumes; of methanol and 10 volumes of ammonium \nhydroxide. \nc y :\nTest'solution. Transfer a quantity of cream containing 50 nag \nof Silver Sulphadiazine to a 50-ml conical flask, add 4 ml of \nammonium hydroxide and mix until a smooth paste has been \nobtained. Add 16 ml of methanol, shake for 5 minutes, and\nfilter. ■ \n?.\nReference solution. Dissolve 35 mg of silver .sulphadiaz^ \nIPRS in-4 ml of ammonium hydroxide and add. 16 ml ° \nmethanol.\n3582\nwww.webofpharma.com\nIP 2022\nt to- thé. plate J 0 j-il of each solution. Allow the mobile . \nh ’ to rise 10 cm. Dry the plate in air and examine under \nl^iolet light;at 254 nm. The principal spot in the\nS rnatogram obtained with the test solution corresponds to \n^at in the chromatogram obtained with the reference solution.\n.... 1 y \n1 x ' ' ' . i ’ P\nfeists\n; fl (2 4 24). 4.Ô to 7.0, determined in the supernatant obtained \nfronl5percentw/vofcreamin vwter.\n^¡crôbïàicontamination (2.2.9). 1.0 g is free from#, coli, \n$faphyioç^ \nPseudomonas aeruginosa and 10 g\nis free from Salmonella species and Shigella. '\n’•*^•.¿>0,!wiVn.'#'.'''’4’1,’' ,r\" \n''' \n\" \n'\nOther tests. Comply with the tests stated under Creams.\nSimvastatin\nAssay.'Determine by liquid chromatography (2,4.14).\nSo/vehi mfrMre. Dissolve 100 ml of ammonium hydroxide in \nwater and dilute to 1000 ml with water;.\nTest solution. Transfer a portion of cream containing 10 mg of \nSilver Sulpha,diazine to a 50-ml round-bottom centnfuge tube. \nAdd about 30 mî pjf methanol, tightly seal the tube with a cap\ncontaining an inert line and mix using à vortex mixer for about\n15 seconds! Centrifuge for 15 minutes. Aspirate, and discard \nthe methanol '(Note — Care should be taken to avoid \naspirating any of the residue). Transfer 5.0 ml of the internal \nstandard solution into the tube and add 20 ml of ethanol \n(95 percent). Replace the cap and mix. Heat in a water-bath at \n60° with periodic mixing for 15 minutes to melt and disperse \nthé cream. While the mixture is still hot, transfer 10.0 ml of the \nsolvent mixture to the tube, mix and cool to room temperature. \nTransfer 2.0 ml of the solution to another tube, add 40 ml of \nmobile phase, mix and filter. t .\nInfernal standard solution. A 0.2 per cent w/v-solution of \nsulphamerazine in.the solvent mixture..\nReference solution (a). A Q.l percent w/y solution of. silver \nsulphadiazine IPRS in the solvent mixture.\nReference solution (b). Pipet 10.0 ml of reference solution (a) \ninto a 50-ml test tube. Add 20 ml of ethanol (95 per cent) and \n5.0 ml of the internal standard solution. Pipet 2.0 ml of the \nsolution iritô a 50-ml test tube, add 40 ml of mobile phase and \nnix \n. j •\nShake a quantity of the powdered tablets containing about \n50 mg of Simvastatin with 20 ml of dichlorometharie, filter and\n3584\nwww.webofpharma.com\nrate the filtrate to dryness using a rotary evaporator \nie j water-bath at 40°. On the residue, determine by infrared \nH orption spectrophotometry (2.4.6). Compare the spectrum\n, h that ohtained-with simvas tatinIPRS or with the reference\n^¿tr^pfsiiwastetin: ' \n\\\n■, -\n£\nA. \nDetermine by thin-layer chromatography (2.4 J/XcoaiO \nthe plate with silica gel G.\nMobile phase. A mixture of 60 volumes of methari^^\nrsJmyf\nvolumes of ammonium hydroxide and. 25 \nchloroform. \n„\n■ . . . . .... |\nReference solution fa). A1.0 per cent w/v solutioriofsisomicin g\n/PRS. \n- \n■■ ■■■ -■■■ \n' g\nTest, solution. A. 1.0 per cent w/v solution of the- substances’ |.\nunder examination. .... \n.. o . + ¿A I\nReference solution (b). A mixture of equal volumes ofthetest |\nsolution and reference solution (a). \n■ \n|\nApply to the plate 5 pl of each solution. After dey^qpnient, I\nallow the plate to dry in air, heat it at 110° for, 15 minutes and |\nimmediately spray it with a 1.0 per cent solution of ninhydrin |\nin butanol containing 1.0 per cent :of pyridine: The principal |\nbrown spot 