g of anhydrous disodium hydrogen phosphate and\n5.88 g of sodium citrate in 2000 ml water, adjusted to pH \n8.0 with orthophosphoric acid or sodium hydroxide,\nBi 70 volumes of acetonitrile and’30 \nvolumes of a buffer solution prepared by dissolving \ns, 2.84gofnn/?ydrai/.S' disodium hydrogen phosphate and\n5.88 g of sodium citrate in 2000 ml water, adjusted to pH \n8.0 with orthophosphoric acid or sodium hydroxide, \n- a gradient programme using the conditions given below, \n- flow rate: 1.8 fnl per minute, \n- spectrophotometer set at 266 nin, \n- injectionvolume: 20ul. r;\nTithe?: : Mobile phase A Mobile phase B \n(inmin.)-' (per cent v/v) (per cent v/v)\n' 0 '\n10Q {) .\n■ ■ \n50 \n- \n50\n28 \n0 \n100\n/”;35W-v:;.c Joo \n- . \n- o\nT^7^ntiop time of alendronate is about 7 minutes.\nThe relative retention time with reference to alendronate, for\n’mPurity D and impurity Ais about 1.4 and 1.9 respectively.\nrsference solution (a) and reference solution (b) to\n1 \nthe pc^k due to impurity A and impurity D.\ninject the reterence solution, (b). The test is not valid unless\ne resolution; between the peak.due to alendronate and \nlmPwityDisnot-less than 5.0.\nj$ferehCe solution (a) and the test solution. In the \n°matogram obtained with the test solution, the area of any\npeak corresponding to impurity A multiply by correction factor \n0.4 is not more than the area of the principal peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (a) (0.15 per \ncent), the area of any secondary peak is. not more than the \narea of the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained with \nreference solution (a) (0.1 per cent) and the sum of areas of all \nthe secondary peaks is not more than the area of the principal \npeak in the chromatogram obtained with reference solution \n(a) (0,5 per cent), calculated by area normalization.\nImpurities B and C. Determine by liquid chromatography \n(2.4.14). . . \n. t.t, . . \n.\nTest solution,- Dissolve 50;Q mg of the substance under \