lving 6.8 g of potassium \ndihydrogen orthophosphate in 1000 ml of waler.\n- flow rate: 1.5 ml per minute,\n- spectrophotometer set at 210 nm,\n- injection volume : 2 0 pl.\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the \ncolumn efficiency is not less than 2000 theoretical plates, the \ntailing factor is not more than 1.5 and the relative standard \ndeviation for replicate injections is riot more than 2.0 per cent.\nInject the reference solution and’ the test solution:\nCalcúlate the content of CjoHn^NaCbS by multiplying the\ncontent of CioH12N405S with 1.073.\nTazobactam Sodium intended for use in the manufacture of \nparenteral preparations without a further appropriate \nprocedure for the removal of bacterial endotoxins complies\nwith the following additional requirement.\nBacterial endotoxins (2.2.3), Not more than 0.20 Endotoxin \nUnit per mg of tazobactam sodium, \n...........\nTazobactam Sodium intended for use'in thé manufacture of \nparenteral preparations without d further'appropriate\nsterilisation procedure complies with the following \nadditional requirement. \n,,,.. \n.\nSterility (2.2.11). Complies-with the tesffor sterility. ;\nStorage. Store protected from moisture, at a temperature not \nexceeding 30°. ' \n< \n?■\" '\n3722\nAn\nM.W.: 1564 \nH\nCategory. Glycopeptides antibacterial. \n': \n\\\nTeicoplanin is a mixture of the glycopeptides produced by the \ngrowth of certain strains of Actinoplanes teichomyceiicussp- \nfermentation product. The 6 principle contents of the mixturé \nare teicoplanin A2-i to A2.5 and teicoplanin A34. ... -.. : ;\nTeicoplanin has a potency of not less than 900 Units permg, \ncalculated on the anhydrous basis and bn sodium'chloride \nfree substances. \n.\nwww.webofpharma.com\nA yellowish, amorphous powder.\nXJJetenuinc by infrared absorption spectfophotometery \niA 6)/<Çompare the. spectrum with that obtained, with\n■^glagfeiJPRS or with the reference spectrum of teicoplanin.\ng flithetest for Compositio