ume: 20 pl.\nTEICOPLANIN\nTime\nMobile phase A\nMobile phase B\n(in min.)\n(per cent v/v)\n(per cent v/v)\n0\n100\n0\n30\n50\n50\n31\n10\n90\n35\n10\n90\n38\n100\n0\nName\nRelative \nretention time\nTeicoplanin A3.1\n0.43\nTeicoplanin A2.i\n0.93\nTeicoplanin A2.2 (retention time about 18 minutes) 1.0\nTeicoplanin A2-3\n1.04\nTeicoplanin A2^\n1.12\nTeicoplanin A2-5\n1.14\nImpurities is more than 1.25\nInject treference solution (a) The test is not valid unless the \nresolution between the peak due to teicoplanin A2.4 and \nteicoplanin A2.5 is not less than 1.0.\nThe relative retention time with respect to Teicoplanin A2.2 \npeak for of groups and impurities with reference to teicoplanin \nA2-2 are\n- Teicoplanin A3 group is less than 0.7,\nand within this group, !\n- Teicoplanin A31i group is less than 1.0,\n- \nTeicoplanin A2.3 group is more than 1 and less than 1.12,\n- \nTeicoplanin A7.4 is about l.l2,\n- \nTeicoplanin A2.5 group is more than 1.12 and less than \n1.25.\n: teicoplanin A2 group is more than 0.7 and less than 1.25\nCalculate the content of the different components using the \nfollowing equations"},{"name":"impurities","text":"=------—----------------- x 100\nSa+'.0.83 x Sb + Sc\nWhere, Sa = sum of the areas of the peaks due to\nteicoplanin A2 group in the chromatogram\nv r x obtained with the test solution;\nSb = sum of the areas of the peaks due to\nteicoplauin A3 group in the chromatogram \nobtained with the test solution; disregard any \npeak due to mesityl oxide;\nSo = sum of the areas of the peaks with a relative\nretention more than 1.25;\nS\\ = sum of the areas of the peaks due to\nteicoplauin A2.] group in the chromatogram \nobtained with the test solution;\nS2 “ area of the peak due to teicoplauin A2-2 in the\nchromatogram obtained with the test solution;\nS3 = sum of the areas of the peaks, due to\n, teicoplauin A2.3 group in the chromatogram\nobtained with the lest solution; . . ..\nS4 = area of the peak due to teicoplauin A2.4 in the\nchr