Injection is a sterile, lyophilized material \nconsisting of Temozolomide with of without excipients. It is \nfilled in a sealed container.\nTemozolomide Injection contains not less than 95.0 per cent \nand not more than 105.0 per cent of the stated amount of \ntemozolomide,C6H()N6O2. -■ ? \n■\nNOTE — Temozolomide is cytotoxic; extra care required to \nprevent inhaling particles and exposing thé 'skin to it.\nThe constituted solution complies with the requirements for \nClarity of:solution, and Particulate matter stated, under \nParenteral Preparations. (Injections). .\nUsual strength. 100 mg. \n. ; P \n, b\n3734\nStorage^ The reconstituted solution stand atroomtempei \nmust be used within 14 frours, including infusion time.\nThe content of the sealed container comply with the \nrequirements stated under Parenteral Preparation (Poyfo \nfor Injection) and with the following requirement. ' ' 'x"},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Temozolomide Injection\nTemozolomide Injection is a sterile, lyophilized material \nconsisting of Temozolomide with of without excipients. It is \nfilled in a sealed container.\nTemozolomide Injection contains not less than 95.0 per cent \nand not more than 105.0 per cent of the stated amount of \ntemozolomide,C6H()N6O2. -■ ? \n■\nNOTE — Temozolomide is cytotoxic; extra care required to \nprevent inhaling particles and exposing thé 'skin to it.\nThe constituted solution complies with the requirements for \nClarity of:solution, and Particulate matter stated, under \nParenteral Preparations. (Injections). .\nUsual strength. 100 mg. \n. ; P \n, b\n3734\nStorage^ The reconstituted solution stand atroomtempei \nmust be used within 14 frours, including infusion time.\nThe content of the sealed container comply with the \nrequirements stated under Parenteral Preparation (Poyfo \nfor Injection) and with the following requirement. ' ' 'x"},{"name":"Identification","text":"A. Disperse a quantity óf injection containing 50 mg of \ntemozolomide methylene chloride with the aid of ultrasound \nfor 30 minutes and filter.Evaporate the filtrate under a stream \nof nitrogen to dryness. On.the residue, determine by. infrared \nabsorption spectrophotometry.(2.4.6). Compare the spectrum \nwith that obtained with temozolomide IPRS treated in similar \nmanner or with the reference spectrum of temozolomide.\nB. In the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with the test solution corresponds to the .peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (a).\nA. Determine by infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2-4.6). \nCompare the spectrum with that obtained with teneligliptin \nhydrobromide hydrate IPRS or with the reference spectrum \nof teneligliptin hydrobromide hydrate. / .\nB. In the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with the test solution corresponds to the peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with the réference solution.\nHydrobromic acid content. Nbt less than 28.0 per cent w/w \nand not more than 34.0 per cent w/w; calculated on the \nanhydrous basis, determine by liquid chromatography\n3735\nwww.webofpharma.com\nTENELIGLIPTIN’HYDROBROMIDE HYDRATE\n(2.4-14), as described under: Assay with, following \nmodifications.: \n: >: ' \nE ••-.bi:;?\nReference solution.. A 0.003 per cent w/v solution of \nhydro bromicac id IPRSin'the¡Solventmixture. \n-Em ■\nCalculate the content ofHBr, :'\" r ' \ni/'\nEnantiomeric parity. Not more than 0.5 per cent. Determine \nby liquid chromatography (2.4.14). \n: \n-\nTest, solution. Dissolve about 50 mg of the substance tinder \nexamination in 25.0 m\\o£ethanol. \\ \n, u; \n' r\nReference solution (a). A 0.02 per cent w/v solution1 of R- \nisomerlPRS [{(2R,4R)-4-[4f3-Methyl-l-phenyl-lH-pyrazol- \n5~yl)piperazine-l ~yl]pyrrolidine-2-yl}(l, 3-thiazolidine-3- \nyl)methanone hemipentahydrobromide hydrate IPRS] in\nethanol: ■..■-oy G.’- . \n<\nReference solution (b). Weigh about 100 mg of teneligliptin\nhydrobromide hydrate IPRS to a 50-ml v