with the thst solution correspond to the peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with the reference solution.\nC. Specific optical rotation (see Test). \n: . \n:\nD. A 5 per cent w/v solution gives reaction (A) of sodium \n(2.3.i)/; \n:\nTests \"• •\nN, A-Dimethylaniline (2.3.21). Not more than 20 ppm,\npH (2.4.24). 2.5 to 4.0, determined in à1.0 per cent w/V solution \noftiearcillin. \n’\nSpecific optical rotation (2.4.22). + 181.0°to + 197.0°, \ndetermined in a 1.0 percent w/v solution prepared by dissolving \n6.9 g of monobasic sodium phosphate ya. 800 ml. of \\ water. \nadjusted to pH 6.4 with 10 M sodium hydroxide wad dilute to\n1000 ml with water. \n;\nRelated substances. Determine .by liquid . chromatography \n(2.4.14). \n'■...............................................  ■\nTest solution. Dissolve 50 mg of the substance under \nexamination in 20 ml of mobile phase A and dilute to 50.0 ml. \nwith mobile phase A. \n; ■ \n. = \n. :\n37961\nReference solution. A0.002 per cent w/v solution of \nmonosodium monohydrate IPRSvn. mobile phase: A. y ;f.\nChromatographic system\n- a stainless steel column 25 cm x 4 mm,packed wi^\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 pm),\n- \nmobile phase: A. a buffer solution prepared by \ndissolving \\ 3 » ol dibasic ammonium phosphate \nwater, adjusted to pH 7.0 with orthbphbsphbric acid \nanddiluteto 1000 ml with water,\n; : \nB. a mixture of 5 0 volumes ^methanol\nand 50 volumes of mobile phase A, . < / h;.;. . .- y.\n- a gradient programme using the conditions given below\n- \nflow rate: 1ml per minute, \n.-¡mum?\n- spectrophotometer set at 220 nm, \n- injection volume: 20 pl.\nTime\nMobile phase A\nMobile phase B\n(in min.)\n(per cent v/y) ,\n. (per cent v/v)\n0\n100\n0\n30\n30\n70;\n40'\n30\n70\n45\n100\n0\nName \nRelative\nretention time\nTiearcillin \n0.95,1.0\nTicarcillinrelatedcompoundA1 \n2.1\n'.Decarboxy tiearcillin; (2,5-3,3-dimethyI-7-oxo-6[[(thiophen-3yi) \nacetyl]-4j-thia-azabicycIo[3,2,0]heptane-2-qarboxyIic acid. <