the areas of all other secondary peaks is not more than 5 \ntimes the area of the. principal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with reference solution (a) (1.0 per cent).\nOther tests. Comply .with the tests stated under Capsules. ,\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14)^\nTest solution. Dissolve a quantity of the.mixed contents of 20 \ncapsules containing about 50 mg of Tramadol Hydrochloride \nin 150 ml ofthe mobile phase withthe aid of ultrasound and \ndilute to 200 ml with the mobile phase, filter. f■; '■■■'■ ■' ' \n’ 1 '\nReference solution (a). A 6.025 per cent w/v solution of \ntramadol hydrochloride IPRS in the mobile phase.\nReference solution (b). A solution containing 0.0015 per cent \nw/v each of tramadol hydrochloride IPRS and tramadol \nimpurity A IPRS in the mobile phase.\nUse the chromatographic system as described under Related\nsubstances. \n1\nInject reference solution (b). The test is'not’valid unless the \nresolution between the peaks due to tramadol impurity À and \ntramadol hydrochloride is not less than 3.0.\nInject reference solution (a) and the test solution.\nCalculate the content of Ci6H25NO2,HC1 in the Capsules.\nTramadol Prolonged-release Tablets\nTramadol Sustained-release Tablets, Tramadol Extended- \nrelease Tablets\nTramadol. Prolonged-release Tablets manufactured by \ndifferent manufacturers, 'whilst complying . withr the \nrequirements of the monograph, are not interchangeable, as \nthe dissolution profile of the products of different \nmanufacturers may not be the same.\nTramadol Prolonged-release Tablets contains not less than \n95.0 per cent and not more than 105.0 per cent of the stated \namountof tramadol hydrochloridc,Cl6H,5NO2,HCl.\nUsual strengths. 50 mg; lOOmg.\nA. Determine by thin-layer chromatography (2.4.17), using \nthe plate coated with silica gel GF254:'r ' \n1 : ! ; : : f ■\nMobile phase. A mixture of T volume: of arthydroüs formià \nacid, 50 volumes of acetone and : 50 volumes Of methanol.\nTest solution. Disperse a quantity of the powdered tablets \ncontaining 50 mg of tramadol hydrochloride with 25 ml of \nmethanol, shake for 10 minutes; filter (such as Whatman \nGF/A). ■ \n- \nm:.\n3841\nwww.webofpharma.com\nTRAMADOL PROLONGED-RELEASE TABLETS\nReferencesolution. A 0 ;2 ‘per cent w/ysolution : of tramadol \nhydrochloride IPRS vn methanol. ■ 'tsjjc A; !=• n;.-u: aÂ lo\nApply to the plate 10 pl of each solution. Allow the mobile \nphase to rise Ï 5 cm. Dry the plate m air and expose to iodine \nvapour lintiTthe spots appear arid examine in daylight. The \nprincipal spot in the.chromatp^ani.obtained with the..test \nsolution corresponds to that in the chromatogram obtained \nwith référence solution. \n■:t'\nJjnok; A. ■■ ;b<h.ioinmiCi : !■ > g'\" m. ;j .; A..- \nBr; Jn.rthe;,Assay,z the principalpcakin the chromatogram \nobtained with the test solution corresponds to the peak in the \nchromatogram obtained witri the reference solution.\nTests - — A \nAV A gorm'u. -wv-ag. vaavA\nDissolution (2.5/2)!/'Complies with the test stated under \nTablets.........................'/ :,A:A A Al: A; AA G : \n.'.A r\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography \n,#i4>: \n! ..... .\nTest solution.. Disperse a quantity of the powdered tablets \ncontaining 0.5 g of Tramadol Hydrochloridc with SO ml of \nmobile phase, mix with the aid of ultrasound, cool, add sufficient \nmobile phase to produce 100 ml and filter through a glass­\nfibre filter paper (such as'Whatman GF/A). '/' \n'\nReference soZwfi'bnfri). bilufe 2.0 ml of the test solution to\n100.0 ml with the mobile phase and further dilute 1.0 ml of the \nsolution to 10.0 ml with the mobile phase.\nReference solution (ri). A 0.0015 per cent w/v solution of \ntramadol impurity .A IPRS f(IRS,_2^R)-2-[fdimç.thylaminp) \nmethyl]-l-(3-niethoxyphenyl)cyclohexan6l IPRS) in the \nmobilephase. \n'\nReference1 solution (c). À 0.Ô015 per cent w/v solution each of\ntramadol hydrochloride IPRSxnA tramadol impurity A IPRS \n(( 1 RS, 2 SR )- 2- [(d ime thy I am ino) me thy I] -1 -(3- \nmethoxyphenylfcyclohéxanol IPRS) in the mobile phase.\nChromatographic system \n; i ,\n- a stainless steel column 25 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\noctadecylsilanc bonded to porous silica (5 pm),\n- mobile phase: a mixture of 1 volume of tnfluorôacetic\nacid , 30 volumes of acetonitrile and 69<v01Umes of \nwater,\n- flow rate: 1 ml per minute, \n..... . <a-.^\n- spectrophotometer set at 271 nm, ... .Jr . ... a ;\n- injection volume; 20 pl. / -, : :.. n ;\nInject reference soluti"}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/trandolapril","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Trandolapril"},"edition":"ip-2010","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Trandolapril\nC24H34N20s\nMol. Wt. 430.5\nTrandolapril is (2S,3aR,7as)-1 [(5)-2-[[(8)-1-(ethoxycarbonyl)-\n3-phenylpropyl]amino]-1-oxo-propyl]octahydro-1H-indole-2-\ncarboxylic acid.\nwww.webofpharma.com\nTRANDOLAPRlL\nTrandolapril contains not less than 98.5 per cent and not more\nthan 101.5 per centofC24H34N20s,calculated onthe dried basis.\nCategory. Antihypertensive.\nDescription. A white to offwhite crystalline powder."},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Trandolapril\nC24H34N20s\nMol. Wt. 430.5\nTrandolapril is (2S,3aR,7as)-1 [(5)-2-[[(8)-1-(ethoxycarbonyl)-\n3-phenylpropyl]amino]-1-oxo-propyl]octahydro-1H-indole-2-\ncarboxylic acid.\nwww.webofpharma.com\nTRANDOLAPRlL\nTrandolapril contains not less than 98.5 per cent and not more\nthan 101.5 per centofC24H34N20s,calculated onthe dried basis.\nCategory. Antihypertensive.\nDescription. A white to offwhite crystalline powder."},{"name":"Identification","text":"A. Determine by infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2.4.6).\nCompare the spectrum with that obtained with trandolapril\nRS or with the reference spectrum oftrandolapril.\nB. In the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram\nobtained with the test solution corresponds to the peak in the\nchromatogram obtained with the reference solution.\nA. In the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram\nobtained with the test solution corresponds to the peak in the\nchromatogram obtained with the reference solution.\nB. When examined in the range of200 nm to 400 nm (2.4.7), a\n0.05 per cent w/v solution in 0.1 M hydrochloric acid shows\nan absorption maximum as obtained with trandolapril RS of\nthe same concentration."},{"name":"Tests","text":"Specific optical rotation (2.4.22). -16.so to -18.5°, determined\non 2.0 per cent w/v solution in ethanol (95 per cent).\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography\n(2.4.14).\nTest solution. Dissolve 100 mg of the substance under\nexamination in 100 ml ofthe mobile phase.\nReference solution. A 0.0005 per cent w/v solution of\ntrandolapril RS in the mobile phase.\nChromatographic system\n-\na stainless steel column 25 cm x 4.6 mID, packed with\noctylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 !-lm),\n-\nmobile phase: a mixture of60 volumes ofbuffer solution\nprepared by dissolving 6.71 g of monobasicpotassium\northophosphate in 1000 ml of water, 35 volumes of\nacetonitrile and 5 volumes of methanol, adjusted to\npH 4.0 with orthophosphoric acid,\nflow rate. I ml per minute,\n-\nspectrophotometer set at 210 nm,\ninjection volume. 20 !-ll.\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the\nrelative standard deviation for replicates injections is not more\nthan 5.0 per cent.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution. In the\nchromatogram obtained with the test solution, the area ofany\nsecondary peak is not more than the area ofthe principal peak\nin the chromatogram obtained with the reference solution (0.5\nper cent) and the sum ofthe areas of all the secondary peaks\nis not more than twice the area of the principal peak in the\nchromatogram obtained with the reference solution (1.0 per\nHeavy metals (2.3.13).1.0 g complies with the limit test for\nheavy metals, Method B(20 ppm).\nSulphated ash (2.3.18). Not more than 0.1 percent.\nwww.webofpharma.com\nIP 2010\nLoss on drying (2.4.19). Notmore than 0.5 percent, determined\non 1.0 g by drying at 50° for 3 hours under vacuum.\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nTest solution. Dissolve 10 mg of the substance under\nexamination in 100.0 ml ofthe mobile phase.\nReference solution. A 0.01 per cent w/v solution of\ntrandolapril RS in the mobile phase.\nChromatographic system\na stainless steel column 15 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 !-lm) (Such\nas Inertsil CI8),\nmobile phase: a mixture of52 volumes ofbuffer solution\nprepared by dissolving 6.71 g ofmonobasicpotassium\northophosphate in 1000 ml of water, 43 volumes of\nacetonitrile and 5 volumes of methanol, adjusted to\npH 4.0 with orthophosphoric acid,\n-\nflow rate. 1 ml perminute,\nspectrophotometer set at 210 nm,\ninjection volume. 20 !-ll.\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the\ntailing factor is not more than 2.0 and the relative standard\ndeviation for replicate injections is not more than 2.0 per cent.\nInject the test solution and the reference solution.\nCalculate the content ofCz4H34NzOs.\nStorage. Store protected from light and moisture.\nTrandolapril Tablets\nTrandolapril Tablets contain not less than 90.0 per cent and\nnot more than 110.0 per cent of the stated amounts of\ntrandolapril, C24H34N20s.\nUsual strengths. 1 mg; 2 mg.\nApparatus No.1,\nMedium. 500 ml ofwater,\nSpeed and time. 50 rpm and 45 minutes.\n2248\nIP 2010\nWithdraw a suitable volume ofthe medium and filter.\nDetermine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nTest solution. Dilute the filtrate, if necessary, with the\ndissolution medium.\nReference solution. Dissolve an accurately weighed quantity\nof trandolapril RS in the mobile phase and dilute with\ndissolution medium to obtain a solution having a known\nconcentration similar to the test solution.\nUse chromatographic system as described underAssay using\n100 III injection volume.\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the\nrelative standard deviation for replicate injections is not more\nthan 2.0 per cent.\nInject the test solution and the reference solution.\nCalculate the content ofCZ4H34NzOs.\nD. Not less than 80 per cent of the stated amount of\nCZ4H34NzOs.\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography\n(2.4.14).\nNOTE-Use fi-eshly prepared solutions.\nTest solution. Disperse a quantity of powdered tablets\ncontaining about 10 mg ofTrandolapril in 10.0 ml ofthe mobile\nphase.\nReference solution. A 0.001 per cent w/v solution of\ntrandolapril RS in the mobile phase.\nChromatographic system\na stainless steel column 25 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\noctylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 11m) (Such as\nACEC8),\nmobile phase: a mixture of60 volumes ofbuffer solution\nprepared by dissolving 6.71 g ofmonobasic potassium\northophosphate anhydrous in 1000 ml of wate]; 35\nvolumes of acetonitrile and 5 volumes of methanol,\nadjusted to pH 4.0 with orthophosphoric acid,\n-\nflow rate. 1ml per minute,\nspectrophotometer set at 210 nm,\ninjection volume. 20 Ill.\nInject the reference solution. The relative standard deviation\nfor replicate injections is not more than 5.0 per cent. .\nInject the test solution and the reference solution. Run the\nchromatogram 5 times the retention time ofthe principal peak.\nIn the chromatogram obtained with the test solution the area\nofany secondary peak is not more than the area ofthe principal\npeak in the chromatogram obtained with the reference solution\n(1.0 per cent) and the sum of the areas of all the secondary\npeaks is not more than twice the area ofthe principal peak in\n2249\nwww.webofpharma.com\nTRANDOLAPRIL TABLETS\nthe chromatogram obtained with the reference solution (2.0\nper cent).\nUniformity of content. Comply with the test stated under\nTablets.\nDetennine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14), as described\nunder Assay with the following solutions.\nTest solution. Disperse one tablet in the mobile phase, dilute\nto obtain a solution containing 0.005 per centw/v oftrandolapril\nin the mobile phase and filter.\nReference solution. Dissolve an accurately weighed quantity\noftrandolapril RS in the mobile phase and dilute to obtain a\nsolution having a known concentration similar to the test\nsolution.\nCalculate the content ofCZ4H34NzOs in the tablet.\nWater (2.3.43). Not more than 7.0 per cent, determined on\n0.5 g.\nOther tests. Comply with the tests stated under Tablets.\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14"}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/travoprost-eye-drops","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Travoprost Eye Drops"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Travoprost Eye Drops\nTravoprost Eye Drops contains not less than 9Ó.0 per cent \nand not more than 110,0 per cent of the stated amount of \ntravoprost, C26H35F3O6.\nUsual strength. 40 pg per, ml."},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Travoprost Eye Drops\nTravoprost Eye Drops contains not less than 9Ó.0 per cent \nand not more than 110,0 per cent of the stated amount of \ntravoprost, C26H35F3O6.\nUsual strength. 40 pg per, ml."},{"name":"Identification","text":"A. In the Assay, the principal peak in thè chromatogram \nobtained with'the test solution corresponds to the peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with the reference solution;\n3850\n.................................................................................  _ lp2(£\nB. Determine by thin-layer chromatography (2.4.1 \n. 7\nthe plate with silica gel G.\nMobile phase. A mixture of 50 volumes of be/zz^ \nvolumes \n,\nTest solution. Extract eye drops containing about 0.8 m \nTravoprost with 20.0 ml of chloroform in a separating' \nCollect the chloroform layer in a 250 ml beaker. Give \nwashings with chloroform. Evaporate the chloroform Uyeiis \ndryness and add 3.0 ml of methanol.\nReference.vo/mZ/ou. Dissolve 20 mg of-frdybprbsrTpj^.^^\nml of acetonitrile, sonicate and dilute to 20.0 nil with \nDilute 5.0 ml of the solution to 20.0 ml with methanol. .\nApply to the plate 20 pl of each solution. Allow the Mobile \nphase to rise 8 cm. Dry the plate and spray with 40. percen; \nw/v solution, of phosphomolybdic acid dx.ethanol,]^^ \nplate at 110° for 15 minutes and examine immediately The \nprincipal spot in the chromatogram obtained with the test \nsolution corresponds to the spot obtained with the reference \nsolution.\n^¿^{a^T^ntion time with respect to travoprost for 5,6- \nj^-^oprost' is 1 -1 [NOTE —Travoprost IPRS contains a\nsnial!percentage ofthe 5,6- trans isomer].\n\"solution (a). The test is not valid unless the \n^l^flonf’oKtiitnpd between travoprost and 5,6-trans\nnot less than 1.5. The column efficiency is not \nless thari 20d0 theoretical plates, the tailing factor is not more\nthan 2-0 and the relative standard deviation for replicate \ninjections is not more than 2.0 per cent."},{"name":"Tests","text":":■ . \n■' ;\npH(2.4.24).5.7to6.3. \n\" < ’ . \n.\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatographv \n(2.4.14). \n• ' \nv ••\nSolvent mixture. Equal volumes of water arid acetonitrile.\nTest solution. Dilute the eye drops, if necessary with the \nsolvent mixture, to produce a solution containing 6.004 per \ncent w/v of travoprost. ■' \n■■\nReference solution (a). A 0.004 per cent w/v solution of\ntravoprost IPRS in the solvent \"mixture. ; ; J : ■1\nReference solution (b). Dilute 1.0 ml of reference solution (a) \nto 10.0 ml with the solvent mixture.\nChromatographic system \npa p\n- a stainless steel column 25 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous \nsilica (5 pm) (Such as Hypersil ODS),\n- column temperature: 35°,\n- sample temperature: 10°, \n.iHC'fip'A’* •1\n- mobile phase A: a buffer solution prepared by\ndissolving 1.5 g of 1-octane sodium sulphonic acid®\n1000 ml pf wdter, adjusted to pH 25 with ortho-\nphosphosric acid, \nryi\nB; a mixture of 80 volumes bfacetonitri^\nand 20 volumes of mobile phase A, \n\\\n- a gradient programme using the conditions giyen bekA\n- flow rate: 1 ml per minute, -\n- spectrophotometer set at 220 nm,\n■- injection volume: 100 pl. \nVA-\nwww.webofpharma.com\nil#-\nMobile phase A\nMobile phase B\n1 (per cent v/v)\n(per cent v/v)\n50\n50\n42\n58\nA{<5ÓA\n50\n50\nF c0^umn ^)r at ^east m’ni,tes with the mobile \np^seatthe initial composition:\n50\n50\nInject Reference solution (b) and the test solution. In the \ncluroinatogram obtained with the test solution the area of any\nsecondary peak is not more than 0.4 times the area of the \nprincipalpeak in the chromatogram obtained with reference \nsolution (b) (4.0 per cent) and the sum of areas of all the \nsecondary peaks is not more than 0.6 times the area of the \nprincipal peak in the chromatogram obtained with reference\n(6'Opercent).\nOther tests. Comply with the tests stated under Eye\nDrops. ; \n.\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14) as\ndescribed under test for Related substances.\nInject reference solution (a) and the test solution.\nCalculate the content ofC^JTT'TT-\nStorage. Store at a temperature not exceeding 30°."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/travoprost","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Travoprost"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Travoprost"},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Travoprost"},{"name":"TRAVOPROST","text":"Travoprost is (5Z)-7-[(lE,2E,3E,55)-3,5-dihydroxy-2-[(lE,3E)- \n3-hydroxy-4-[3-(trifluromethyl)phenoxy]-1 -butenyl]- \ncyclopentyl]-5 -heptenoic acid 1-methylethyl ester.\nTravoprost contains not less than 96.0 per cent and not more \nthan 102.0 per cent of C26H35F306i calculated on the anhydrous \nbasis.\nCategory. Antiglaucoma.\nDescription. A colourless to yellowish oil.\nA. Determine by infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2.4.6). \nCompare the spectrum with that obtained with travoprost IP RS \nor with the reference spectrum of travoprost.\nB. In the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with the test solution corresponds to the peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with the reference solution.\nAppearance of solution. A1.0 per cent w/v solution in ethanol\n(95 per cent) is not more intensely coloured than reference \nsolution YS7 (2.4.1).\nSpecific optical rotation (2.4.22). + 52° to + 58°, determined on \n2.0 per cent w/v solution in ethanol at 365 nm.\nRelated substances. Not more than 3.5 per cent of 5,6-trans- \ntravoprost.\nDetermine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nTest solution. Dissolve 100 mg of the substance under \nexamination in acetonitrile and dilute to 100.0 ml with water.\nReference solution. Dissolve 10 mg of travoprost IPRS in\nacetonitrile and dilute to 100.0 ml with water. Dilute 1.0 ml of \nthe solution to 20.0 ml with water.\nUse chromatographic system as described under Assay.\nThe relative retention time with reference to travoprost for \n5,6-trans-travoprost is about 1.06.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution. In the \nchromatogram obtained with the test solution, the area of any \nsecondary peak is not more than the area of the principal peak \nin the chromatogram obtained with the reference solution \n(0.5 per cent) and the sum of the areas of all the secondary \npeaks is not more than 12 times the area of the principal peak \nin the chromatogram obtained with the reference solution \n(6.0 per cent).\nWater (2.3.43). Not more than 1.0 per cent, determined on \n0.1 g.\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nTest solution. Dissolve. 100 mg of the substance under \nexamination in acetonitrile and dilute to 100.0 ml with water.\n3849\nwww.webofpharma.com\nReference solution. Dissolve 10 mg' of travoprost IPRS in \na6'etoi?/7n7«an.d dilute to 10.0 ml with wizZez: \n. \n/\nChromatographic system '■ - ■ \nC ; ;\na stainless steel column 25 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\n. octadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5. pm), (Such\nas Hypersil ODS),\n- column temperature: 50°,\n- mobile phase: A. a mixture of 66 volumes of buffer\nsolution prepared by diluting 1 ml of orthophosphoric \nacid to 1000 ml with water, adjusted to pH 5.0 with 1M \nsodium hydroxide, 30 volumes of acetonitrile and 4\n... volumes of propanol-2-ol,\nB. a mixture of 80 volumes ofacetonitrile, \n4 volumes of propanol-2-ol and 16 volumes of water, \n- a gradient programme using the conditions given below,\n— flow rate: 1 ml per minute, \n- spectrophotometer set at 220 nm, \n- injection volume: 50 pl.\nTime\nMobile phase A\nMobile phase B\n(in min.)\n(per cent v/v)\n(per cent V/V)\n0\n100\n’ \no\n5\n80\n20 '\n50\n80\n20 ’ ''\n70\n0\nloo\n80\n0\n100.\n82\n100\n■ 0\n90\n100\n0\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the \nresolution between the peaks due to travoprost and 5-trans- \ntravoprost is, not less than 1.5, the theoretical plates; is not \nless than 1500, the tailing factor is not more than 2.0 and the \nrelative,standard deviation for replicate injections is not more \nthan 2.0 per cent.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\nCalculate the content of C26H35F3O6.\nStorage. Store protected from moisture, at a temperature \nbetween 2° and 8°."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/trazodone-hydrochloride","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Trazodone Hydrochloride"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Trazodone Hydrochloride\nCiÄ2C]N5O,HCI\nMol. Wt 408.3\n• Trazodone Hydrochloride is l,2,4-Triazolo[(4,3-a]pyridin- \n3(2H)-one, 2-[3-[4-(3-chlorophenyl)-l -piperazinyl]propyl]-,\nm°nohydrochloride.\nTRAZODONE HYDROCHLORIDE\nTrazodone Hydrochloride contains not less than 98.0 per cent \nand not more than 102.0 per cent of C19H22C1N5O,HC1, \ncalculated on the dried basis.\nCategory. Antidepressant.\nDescription. A white to off white, crystalline powder.\nA. Determine by infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2.4.6). \nCompare the spectrum with that obtained with trazodone \nhydrochloride IPRS or with the reference spectrum of \ntrazodone hydrochloride.\nB. In the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with the test solution corresponds to the peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with the reference solution.\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography \n(2.4.14).\nSolvent mixture. 80 volumes of mobile phase A and 20 volumes \nof mobile phase B.\nTest solution. Dissolve 50 mg of the substance under \nexamination in the solvent mixture and dilute to 50,0 ml with \nthe solvent mixture.\nReference solution (a). A 0.0001 per cent w/v solution of\ntrazo do ne hydrochloride IPRS in the solvent mixture, ..\nReference solution (b). A solution containing 0.0001 per cent \nw/v, each of, trazodone related compound C IPRS and \ntrazodone related compound D IPRS in reference solution\nChromatographic system \n<\n- a stainless steel column 7.5 cm x.4.6 mm, packed,with\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (3.5 pm),\n- mobile phase: A. a O.Olper cent v/v solution of\ntriethylamine in water, \n. \n,\nB. a O.Olper cent y/v solution of \ntriethylamine in' acetonitrile,\n- a gradient programme using the conditions given below, \n- flow rate: 2 ml per minute,\n- spectrophotometer set at 254 nm,\ninjection volume: 10 pl.\nTime\nMobile phase A\nMobile phase E\n(in min.)\n(per cent v/v)\n(per cent v/v)\n0\n80\n20\n12\n; '?.:3i2';X\n, ’ ' 68 ' '\n. 12.01\n. 80\n20\n15\n■ 80\n20\n3851\nwww.webofpharma.com\nTRAZODONE HYDROCHLORIDE\nretention time factor\nName, \nRelative Correction\nTriazolopyridinone1\n0.1\n2.08\nTrazodone Y-oxide2\n0.40\nDeschloro trazodone3\n0.65\n1.41 ■\nTrazodone related compound C\n0.96\n—\nTrazodone\n1.0\n—\nTrazodone related compound D\n1.1\n— . ■■■\n4-Ethyl trazodone4\n1.4\n—\nTrazodone isobutyl ether analog5 2.0 .X,\nBispiperazine analog6\n2.1\n0.77\n'[l,2,4]Triazolo[4,3-a]pyridin-3.(2J7)-one,\n24-(3-Chiorophenyl)-r-[3-(3-oxo-[l,2,4]triazolo[4,3-a]pyridin-2(3iZ)- \nyl)p