eference \nsolution (a) (1-0 per cent). Ignore any peak with an area less \nthan 0.5 times the area of the principal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with reference solution (a) (0.05 per cent).,\n385.2 \nfiMlMMil\nTRAZODONE TABLETS\n$20$\n..............................................................-...........................■■\nLimit of Trazodone related compound F and Cyclophosphan&r | \nrelated compound A. Determine by liquid chromatogra^ < ?\nj impound F peak, and not less than 50 for the \n^^hosnba111^6 related compound Apeak and the relative \n^^^(fcwiation Tor replicate injections is not more than \n^^¿¿nfforeach of trazodone related compound F and \n$c|0$psph.^dc related comPound A Peak-\nMedium. 900 ml of 0.01 M hydrochloric acid,\nSpeed and time. 50 rpm and 60 minutes.\nmass spectrometry (2.4.39)\nNOTE—Perform this test only if trazodone related|\nWithdraw a suitable volume of the medium and filter.\nF and cyclophosphamide related compound A are I \nprocess impurities. \n. ■■ \n|\nDetermine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nt tBBtefeience solution and the test solution. In the \nh* matogrambbtairied w’dl dlc test S(dut’on^ the area of any \n^k corresponding to trazodone related compound F and \n^lonhosphainjdc rclated compound A, each of, is not more\nTest solution. Use the filtrate, dilute if necessary, with the \ndissolution medium.\nSolvent mixture. 10 volumes of acetonitrile, 90 volume Of \nwater and 0.1 volume of formic acid.. \n; .. .. ,/ ' j '; <\nReference solution. Dissolve a quantity of trazodone \nhydrochloride IPRS in the dissolution medium and dilute with \nthe same medium to obtain a solution of known concentration \nsimilar to the expected concentration of the test solution.\nTest solution. Dissolve lg of the substance undcrexa"},{"name":"identification","text":"Reference solution (a). An accurately weighed quantity of \ntrazodone hydrochloride IPRS containing 0.0005 per cent \nw/v solution of trazodone in the solvent mixture. Dilute