packed with\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (3.5 urn), (Such\ni: \":i asXTerraMS),\ncolumn temperature:32°, - • T '-Horbenxw.\n- mobile phase: A. abuffer solution prepared by\ndissolving 1.74 g of dipotassium hydro’geri phosphate\n: ;' in 1Ó00 ml of wr/Ze/', adjusted tb pH 6.5 with\norihophosphoric acidf \n'' w,; \n?f:\n: \nB. a mixture of 75 volumèsbfiïdé/ow/nïe\n' and 25 volumes of mobile phase A, :\n■ ■ a gradient programme using the conditions given below,\n- flow rate: 0.8 ml per minute,\n- spectrophotometer set at 210 nm,\n- injection volume: 5 pl.\nMôWMpnâseW ¿\n(per cent v/v)\nMobile phase A\nTime \n(in min.)\n(per cent v/v)\n0\n95\n5 .\n10\n34\n66\n12.5 \n, \n. ç 34\n66\n12.6\n95\n5\n15\n95\n"},{"name":"Tests","text":"Dissolution (2.5.2).\nApparatus No. 2 (Paddle),\nMedium. 1000 ml of 0.01Mhydrochloric acid, \n; -\nVILDAGLIPTIN TABLETS\nSpeed and time. 50 rpm and 30 minutes.\nWithdraw a suitable volume of the rnedium and filter.\nDetermine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).. ? \n,\nTest solution. Use the filtrate, dilute-if necessary, with the \ndissolution medium.\nReference solution. A 0.005 per cent w/v solution of \nvildagliptin IPRS in the dissolution medium.\nChromatographic system\n- a stainless steel column 5 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\noctadecylsilanobonded to porous silica (3.5 pm), (Such \nas Waters XTerra MS 120 A),.\n- column temperature: 35°,\n- mobile phase: a mixture of 90 volumes of a buffer solution\nprepared by dissaving 1.3 g ofpotassium, dihydrogen \nphosphate in 1000 ml of water, adjusted to pH 6.5 with\n10 per cent w/v solution of dipotassium hydrogen \nphosphate and 10 volumes of acetonitrile,\n■ \n- flow rate: 2.5 ml per minute,\n- spectrophotometer set at 210 nm,\n- injection volume: 10 pl.\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the \ntailing factor is not more than 2.0 and the relative standard \ndeviation for replicate injections is not more than 2.0.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\nCalculate the content of C^H^NaC^ in the medium.-\nQ. Not less than 80 per cent of the stated amount of \nC)7H25N3O2.\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography \n(2.4.14). '\nSolvent mixture. 90 volumes of 0.02 M hydrochloric acid \nand 10 volumes of acetonitrile.\nBuffer solution. Dissolve 1.3 g of potassium dihydrogen \nphosphate in 1000 ml of water, adjusted to pH 6.5 with 10 per\ncent w/v .solution of .dipotassium hydrogen phosphate.\nTest solution. Disperse a ¡quantity of powdered tablets \ncontaining 50 mg of vildagliptin in the solvent mixture, with \nthe aid of ultrasound and dilute to 100.0 ml with the solvent \nmixture.\nReference solution (a). ' A 0.05 per cent w/v solution of \nvildagliptin IPRS inthe solvent mixture.\nReference solution (b). Dilute 1.0 ml of reference solution (a) \nto 100.6 ml with the solvent mixture.\nPreference solution (c),. Dilute .5.0.ml of reference solution (b) \nto 50.0,mlwith the solvent mixture. , \n, \n.\nReference solution (df A solution containing 0.05 per cent \nw/v of ■vildagliptin IPRS and 0.0005 per cent w/v, each of, \nvildagliptin impurity A, B and C in the solvent mixture.\n3941\nwww.webofpharma.com\nVILDAGLfI’TIN TABLETS\nas Waters, XTcrra MS I 20 Â),\n- column temperature: 35°, - \n..... j\n- mobile phase: A. a mixture of 40 volumes of the: buffer\n. solution, 60 volumes of water, 1.5 volumes of methanol\n■ and 1.5 volumes of acetonitrile,\nB. à mixture of 40 volumes of the buffer \nsolution, 45 volumes of acetonitrile and 15 volumes of \ni;! miethancrl; 33- cc: c ro\ni a gradicnt programme using thc conditions given below, \n- flow rate: 1.8 ml per minute, \n- spectrophotometer set at 210 nm, ; : \n-injection volume: 10 pl. : \n•; =•■\nMòbile phase B\nMobile phase A\n(per cent v/v)\nTime \n(in min.)\n(per cent v/v)\n..... 0 .\n100 . .\n1\n■ 90 ■ \n...: ,. . .\n3\nName\nRelative \nretention time\nVildagliptin impurityA1 \n: 0.61\ntyB2 : \n0.75\n.^-(S'hydroxy-adainantanrLyl)-! -imino-hexahydro-p