{"en":"Zolpidem Tartrate"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Zolpidem Tartrate\n(Ci9H2iNjÔ)2/C4H6O6 \nMol. Wt. 765.0\nZolpidem Tartrate is bis[X^-dimethyl-2-[6-methyl-2-(4- \nmethÿlphényl)imidazo[r,2-a]pyridine-3-yl]acetaniidej tartrate.\nZolpidem Tartrate contains not less than 98.5 per cent and hot \nmore than 101.0 per cent of (C|9l-I2;N3O)2, C4H6C\\ calculated \non the anhydrous basis. ’ * \n'\nCategory.Sedatives.\nDescription ^ white or almost white crystalline powder.\nt • / ,<•’ \nt' - : ' ; \n. \n• •>: \n-"},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Zolpidem Tartrate\n(Ci9H2iNjÔ)2/C4H6O6 \nMol. Wt. 765.0\nZolpidem Tartrate is bis[X^-dimethyl-2-[6-methyl-2-(4- \nmethÿlphényl)imidazo[r,2-a]pyridine-3-yl]acetaniidej tartrate.\nZolpidem Tartrate contains not less than 98.5 per cent and hot \nmore than 101.0 per cent of (C|9l-I2;N3O)2, C4H6C\\ calculated \non the anhydrous basis. ’ * \n'\nCategory.Sedatives.\nDescription ^ white or almost white crystalline powder.\nt • / ,<•’ \nt' - : ' ; \n. \n• •>: \n-"},{"name":"identification","text":"A. Determine by infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2.4.6). \nCompare the spectrum with that obtained with zolpidem \n^rtraty IPRS or with the. reference spectrum of zolpidem \ntertrate. \n■\n$• A10 per cent w/v solution in methanol gives reaction (c) of \n^ates (2.3.1). \n' \n''' ?'\nTests ...■=<■ \n. \n■ ■■ ■ .\nAppearance of solution . Dissolve 1.0 g of the substance under \nlamination in 4 00 ml of a 0.5 per cent w/v solution of tartaric\nZOLPIDEM TARTRATE\nacid..The.solution is clear (2.4.1), and not more intensely \ncoloured than reference solution YS6 or B YS6 (2.4.1).\nRelated: substances. Determine by liquid chromatography \n(2.4.14).\nTest solution. Dissolve 25 mg of the substance under \nexamination in 50.0 ml of the mobile phase.\nReference solution (af AÛ.01 per .cent w/v ^solution of N,N- \ndimethyl-2-[7-methyl-2-(4-methylphenyl) imidazo[l,2-a] \npyridin~3~yI acetamide IPRS (zolpidem impurity A IPRS) in\nReference solution (b).A 0.05 per cent w/v solution of \nzolpidem tartrate IPRS in the mobile phase.\nReference solution (c). Dilute 1.0 ml of the reference solution\n(b) to 100.0 ml with the mobile phase.\nReference solution (A), To 2.0 ml of reference solution (b),\nadd 10.0 ml of reference solution (a).\nChromatographic system\n- a stainless steel column 15 cm x 3.9 mm, packed with\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (4 pm),.\n- mobile phase: 18 volumes of acetonitrile, 23 volumes\n: .oT methanol and 59 volumes of 0.56 per cent w/v.\nsolution of orthophosphoric acid, adjusted to pH 5.5 \nwith triethylamine, . . ...\n- flow rate: 1.5 ml per minute,\n- spectrophotometer set at 254 nm,\n- injection volume: 20 pl.\nInject reference solution (d). The test is not valid unless the \nresolution between the peaks due to. zolpidem impurity A and \nzolpidem tartrate is not less than 2.0.\nInject reference solution (c) and the test solution. In the \nchromatogram obtainedwith\"the test solution, the area of any \nsecondary peak’is not more than 0.2 times the area of the peak \nin the chromatogram obtained with reference solution (c) \n(0.2 per cent) and the sum of the areas of all the secondary \npeaks is not more than the area pf the peak in the. chromatogram \nobtained with reference solution (c) (TO per cent). Ignore any \npeak with a relative retention time of 0.16,to the. zolpidem peak, \ncorresponding to tartaric acid and any-secondary peak \nwith an area less, than 0.05 times the area of the peak in \nthe chromatogram obtained with reference solution (c) \n(0.05 per cent). ■'\nSulphated ash (2.3.18). Not more than 0.1 percent. • b - '■ ■■■'\nWater (2.3.43). Not more than 3.0 per cent, determined on \n0.5g. \n-s-iuP-s TfPPs Avk sP ib -\nAssay. Dissolve Ô.3 g in a mixture of 20 ml of anhydrous \nacetic acid and 20 ml of acetic anhydride. Titrate with 0JM \nperchloric acid, determining; the end point potentiometrically\n(2.4.25). Carry out a blank titration \nv\n4003\nwww.webofpharma.com\nZOLPIDEM TARTRATE PROLONGED-RELEASE TABLETS\n1 miof 0. IM perchloric acid is equivalent to 0.03824 g of \nh./•> / -mm :\nStorage. Store protected from light and moisture, at ;a \ntemperature not exceeding 30°.\nZolpidem Tartrate Prolonged-release\nZolpidem Tartrate Prolonged-release Tablets manufactured \nby different manufacturers, whilst complying wjth, the \nrequirements of the monograph, are.notinterchangeable,as \nthe dissolution profile of the products of different \nmanufacturers may not be the same.\nZolpidem Tartrate Prolonged release Tablets contain not less \nthan 90.0 per cent and hot more than 110.0 per cent of the \nstated amount of zolpidem tartrate, C42H48N6O8.\nUsual strengths. 6.25 mg, 12.5 mg\nIn the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained \nwith the test solution (b) corresponds to the peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (b)i\nShakeíáj quantity of the powdered tablets containing 0.1 g of \nZolpidem Tartrate with 40 ml oí methanol, filter and evaporate \nthe fíltrate to dryness. The residue complies with the following\n'-a \n; \n4 ■ ;T\nA: \nDetermine by infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2.4.6). \nCbniparë the spectrum with that obtained with zolpidem \ntartrate IPRS or with the reference spectrum of zolpidem \ntartrate. ■\nB. In the Assay, the priricipal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with the test solution corresponds to the peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with the reference solution. -\nTests r\"\nDissolution (2.5.2).\nApparatus No. 2 (Paddle),\nMedium. 900 ml of 0.01 M hydrochloric acid,\nSpeed and time. 50 rpm and 30 minutes.\nWithdraw a suitable volume of the medium and filter.\nDetermine by liquid chromatography (2.4,14).\n^esi.solution. Use the filtrate,, dilute if necessary, with the \ndissolution medium.\nfyference solution. Dissolve 10 m g oí zolpidem tartrate IPRS \nSufficient znerAimo/toproduce 100.0ml. Dilute the resulting\nZOLPIDEM TABLETS\nsolution with the dissolution: medium to obtain a solution \ncontaining 0.0005 per cent w/v, of zolpidem tartrate.\nUse the chromatographic system described under test for\nRelated substances. \nu 1\ninject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the \nrelative standard deviation for replicate injections is not more \nthan 2.0 per cent.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\nCalculate the content of C42H48N6Os.\nQ. Not less than 75 per cent of the stated amount of \nWA. ■ •■ ■ ■\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography\n(2.4.14). ..... \n.... ■\nTest solution. Disperse a quantity of the powdered tablets \ncontaining 25 mg of Zolpidem Tartrate with 25 ml ofthe mobile \nphase and dilute to 50.0 ml with thè same solvent and filter.\nReference solution (a). A 0.01 per cent w/v solution of N,N- \ndimethyl-2-[7-methyl-2-(4-methylphenyl) imidazo[l,2-a] \npyridin-3-yl acetamide IPRS (zolpidem impurity A IPRS) in\nthe mobile phase. . .............\nReference solution (b). A 0.05 per cent w/v solution of \nzolpidem tartrate IPRS in the mobile phase.\nReference solution (c). Dilute 1.0 ml of the reference solution \n(b) to 100:0 ml with the mobile phase.;\nReference s"},{"name":"Tests","text":"Dissolution (2.5.2). Complies with the test stated under \nTablets. \ne \n•\nUniformity of content. Complies with the test stated under \ntablets.\nDetermine by liquid, chromatography (2.4.14), using the \nchromatographic conditions as described, under Assay.\nTest solution. Transfer one tablet to 25-ml; volumetric flash \nadd about 20.0 ml of a mixture of ethanol and 0.01 M \nhydrochloric acid (4:2) and disperse withtthe aid of ultrasound \nfor20 minutes. Cool and dilute to volume with the same diluent \nand filter, rej ecting the first few ml of the filtrate. Dilute 10.0 ml \nof the filtrate to 25.0 ml; with mobile phase.\ninject reference solution (b) and test solution.\nCalculate the content of C42H4SN6OS in the tablet. ■\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid ¿chromatography \n(2.4.14). . .... \n' \n(.. \n.\nUsing the buffer solution, mobile phase, reference solution \n(a), test solution (b) and chromatographic system as described \nunder Assay. \n'J.\nReference solutipn(b)y Dissolve<a suitable quantity of \nzolpidem related compound A IPRSiaVae reference solution\n(a) to obtain a solution containing 0.0001 per cent*, \nof zolpidem related compound <4. Dilute 1.0 ml of \nsolution to 5;0 ml with mobile phase.\nName. \n? . \nRelative .\nretention time\nkneift\nlactof;.\nO-Aft\nZolpidem acid1 \n0.3 \n:\n1.0 ■Jr\nZolpidem related compound A2 \n0.9\nZolpidem : \n\" \n1.0\nAny unspecified dégradation \nproduct \n”\n- ! Vàÿhj\nTotal impurities \n—\n'2-(6-Methyl-2-p-tolyliinidazo[l,2-a]pyridin-3-yI)acetic acid, T\nW,7V-Dimethyl-2-(7-methyI-2-/>-tolyIimidazo[l,2-a]pyridin-fy^ \nacetamide. \n■■■ ; \n■ \n. 'r\nInject reference solution (b). The test is not valid unless the \nresolution between the peak due to zolpidem related compound \nA and zolpidem is not less than1.5, the relative standard \ndeviation for replicate injections is not more than 2.0 percent \nand tailing factor is not more than 3.0.\nInject test solution (b). The area ofpeak due to zolpidem acid \nis not more than 0.2 per cent, the area of peak due to \nzolpidem related compound A is not more than 0.2 per ceht, \nthe area of peak due to any unspecified degradation product \nis not more than 0.2 per cent, and the sum of all the peaks is \nnot more than 0.5 per cent, calculated by area normalization \nmethod.\nOther tests. Comply with the tests stated under Tablets;\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14). ;\nTest solution (a). Weigh and powder 20 tablets. Disperse a \nquantity of powder containing 50 mg of Zolpidem Tartrate in \n70 ml of a mixture of ethanol nvdO.Ol M hydrochloric acid \n(5:2) stir for 1 hour arid dilute to 100.0 ml with ethanol. Shake \nwell and filter.\nTest solution (b). Dilute test solution (a), suitably with niobile \nphase, to obtam a solution containing 0,01 per cent w/v \nof Zolpidem Tartrate.\nReference solution (a). A 0.05 per cent w/v of zolpidem\ntartrate IPRSva. a mixture of ethanoland 0.01M hydrochloric \nacid(4:l). :•: ■ \n¿¡ftp\nReference solution (b). A 0.01 per cent wlv ofzolpidem \ntartrate 1PRS from the reference solution (a) in mobile phase.\nChromatographic system \n’•\n- a stainless steel column 15 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 pm),,,, \n- column, temperature 40°, \ni\n- \n: mobile phase: a mixture of 11 volumes of a buifcrsolution \n; y prepared by dissolving^ .3 ml of orthophosphoricacid\n4004\nwww.webofpharma.com\n.^3i$lipOp ml of water, adjusted to pH 5.5 with triethylamine,\n^volumes of acetronitrile and 5 volumes of methanol, \n_ flow rate: 1 ml per minute, \n„ spectrophotometer set at 240 nm, \n_ injection volume: 15 pl.\n^ectthdreference solution (b). The test is not valid unless \n^relative standard deviation for replicate injections is not \n^e^ian 2.0 and the tailing factor is not more than 3.0.\n[njectthereference solution (b) and the test solution (b).\nCalculate thc content of C42H4SN6O8 in the tablets.\nStorage. Store protected from light and moisture, at a\nZolpidem Tablets\nZolpidem Tartrate Tablets\nZolpidem Tablets contain not less than 90.0 per cent and riot \nmofe than 110.0 per cent of the stated amount of zolpidem\ntartrate, C^H^NA-\nUsual strengths. 5 mg; 10 mg.\nRelated substaii€es...l)etennine: by -liquidfchromatogi^ \n.(3444)noboe[ni omoiiq^i idt nobab/sb binbcu’.ir\nTest -PoVi/yfoh? \ngribfrHfieJstiir^tanc^^^\nexaminatiq&ip^&gaQbil^phasepp^dilqtetodfiQXl miyyi^Bi \nmobile phase., f . . ... _, ., f■\n.gjsiosj am HI \nto insiHGo Aifjgjy\nReference solution. A solution containing 0.0001 per cents/v \nbf^oriisdiniB^PR^ aifii¥d.d68ib^r\"cJe’ni w/V‘of zon1$j^ \nimpurity A IPRS (l,2-benziso^^ble-3~me:thaiie sxiipj|^v. \nacid IP RS) in the mobile phase.\nUse the chromatographic system as de